From 3b15a0296420c9f815b75e747df38974f7262c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp2: Add the temporal noise reduction algorithm

The ISPP TNR filters each frame against its filtered predecessor with a
noise model calibrated per ISO step, and scales the model block by block
with the gain map the ISP writes along with the frame.

Add an algorithm that programs the ISP gain map with the analogue gain
and fills the ISPP TNR block with the calibration interpolated at that
gain. The conversion follows the Rockchip AIQ MFNR algorithm, including
its gain state ratio, so that the IQ calibration of a sensor applies as
is. The TNR block moves out of the static Ispp parameters.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
